senses.gloss:
ज्वल् JVAL, Ⅰ. P. (E. also Ā.) jvála, blaze, 🞄burn, flame, glow, flash;
 be red-hot: pp. 🞄jvalita, flaming, blazing, flashing, shining;
 🞄cs. jvā̆laya, kindle;
 illuminate;
 intv. jājvalati or jājvalyate, blaze powerfully;
 🞄shine brilliantly. ud, flare up;
 cs. set aflame, 🞄kindle;
 illuminate. pra, begin to blaze or 🞄flash: pp. flaming, blazing;
 shining;
 cs. kindle. 🞄abhi-vi, shine towards. sam, blaze;
 cs. -jvālaya, kindle.

ज्वल jval-a, m. flame;
 -at, pr. pt. burning, 🞄shining etc.;
 m. burning fire.

ज्वाल jvāla, m. flame;
 torch;
 ā, f. illumination;
 🞄flame, bright light: -dhvaja, m. 🞄fire, -mukha, m. (Flame-mouth), kind of 🞄ghost;
 N. of a Brahmarākṣasa, -liṅga, 🞄n. N. of a temple of Śiva.

ज्वलन jval-aná, a. burning;
 shining;
 m. 🞄fire;
 caustic potash;
 n. flaming: -kana, m. 🞄spark.
